      "slug": "trapezoid-panel-g61",
      "term": "Trapezoid panel",
      "definition": "A rectangular piece that is wider at the hem than at the shoulder. For a poncho, front and back panels are near-rectangular. The wider hem falls freely without side seams."
    },
    {
      "slug": "shoulder-seam-g61",
      "term": "Shoulder seam",
      "definition": "The join at the top of front and back panels. On a poncho, seaming leaves a wide neck opening in the centre and the arms pass through the open sides."
    }
